ber of days. It now multiplies them.\n- **`inventory.py`:** `recent(n)` returned one event too many because of an off-by-one slice. It now returns the last `n` events, or an empty list when `n <= 0`.\n- **`members.py`:** `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the comment above it and the tests say five.\n- **`search.py`:** it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`. The function lives in `catalog.text`, so I fixed the import.\n\nThe first batch of edits partly failed, because the edit tool wants each file read first. Only the `books.py` edit went through. I read the other five files and reapplied those edits.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 70216, "requests_cache_write": 80946, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2480266, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 3860, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial18", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 154, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T05:21:29.308044+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 32.578, "t_checker_s": 0.172, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-read-edge", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 3880, "tokens_cache_read": 70216, "tokens_cache_write": 80946, "tokens_fresh": 3863, "tokens_input_uncached": 20, "tokens_main_cache_read": 69184, "tokens_main_cache_write": 80946, "tokens_main_calls": 7, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_output": 3847, "tokens_output": 3860, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 702